[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: .NET11 foundation and SharpUnits completion work packages

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PLAT-NET11
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Stable .NET11 foundation
STATEMENT: The library, conformance runner, tests and demo shall target net11.0 using stable SDK11.0.100 with patch roll-forward and no prerelease selection. Current commands shall resolve the stable SDK and correct target paths while disabled workflows remain manual-only.
COMMENT: User request2026-11-13. Implementation: global.json, four project files, active PowerShell entry points and workflows. Acceptance/evidence: conformance/net11-migration.md. Historical .NET10 evidence is not retitled as .NET11 qualification.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PLAT-FROZEN
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Immutable shared lookup metadata
STATEMENT: Shared SI prefix definitions and fixed metric membership shall use immutable BCL collections while preserving ordinal symbol identity, exact prefix factors and the prior public MetricPrefixes order. C#15 constructor arguments shall preserve the explicit comparer in the metric collection expression.
COMMENT: User-requested language/library reuse, with inferred bounded immutability criterion. Implementation: SiPrefixes and JavaUnitTextFormat. Verification: Net11ModernizationTests (red mutable-catalog witness, case/Unicode checks and seed385,1113), full existing format/prefix regressions and paired Java corpora. No performance claim is inferred from collection choice.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: WP-COMPLETE-1
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Core semantic reconciliation and recoverable operations
STATEMENT: Close remaining quantity, unit, conversion and dimension behavior within an explicit Java/CLR compatibility envelope, with independent arithmetic/converter oracles and typed expected-failure boundaries where callers can recover.
COMMENT: Proposed work package owning60 TCK occurrences. Acceptance, dependencies, library candidates and assertion ownership: docs/package-completion-five.md and conformance/completion-work-packages.json. Native electrical/symbolic and temperature policies must remain intact.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: WP-COMPLETE-2
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: General formatting and parsing
STATEMENT: Reconcile graph formatting/parsing, format families, labels, aliases, cursors, malformed text and culture behavior against pinned Java observations, preserving converter order and complete value/unit/scale observations.
COMMENT: Proposed work package owning11 TCK occurrences. Use existing parsers/BCL facilities or qualified libraries before extending a custom grammar. Native JSONL serialization is a candidate, not an already qualified replacement.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: WP-COMPLETE-3
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Prefixes catalogs and exact factories
STATEMENT: Reconcile prefix metadata, systems of units, obtaining units/quantities and quantity factories, including exact numeric-family preservation, catalog identity and mutation isolation.
COMMENT: Proposed work package owning20 TCK occurrences. Frozen BCL metadata is available; preserve intentionally mutable registry operations. Acceptance and dependencies are in the five-package plan.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: WP-COMPLETE-4
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Services providers and structural interoperability
STATEMENT: Reconcile provider/service selection and structural type assertions using explicit CLR mappings or qualified interoperability adapters; document non-equivalent Java reflection/class behavior without presenting an analogue as Java identity.
COMMENT: Proposed work package owning22 TCK occurrences. Prefer explicit maintained DI/registration facilities where suitable; external discovery requires isolated, deterministic executable evidence.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: WP-COMPLETE-5
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Qualification packaging and release evidence
STATEMENT: Qualify all113 inventoried assertions with revision-bound evidence and review; complete mutation/fuzz/property and platform qualification, consumer/package examples, XML/API engineering documentation and release reproducibility before claiming product completion.
COMMENT: Cross-cutting work package; no duplicate primary ownership of TCK occurrences. Windows/Ubuntu/Java CI gates remain blocked while the user keeps CI disabled. Do not enable or dispatch workflows or promote VERIFIED status merely to satisfy this plan.
